{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014JT5kCQjtWFasBXkwT2num","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\ttitle: Fix a failing check\n3\tdescription: Read a manni meta validation error, map it to the offending field and line, fix it, and confirm green locally.\n4\ttype: troubleshooting\n5\tid: meta-fix\n6\tkeywords:\n7\t  - fix a failing check\n8\t  - error line\n9\t  - required field\n10\t  - parse error\n11\t  - schema not found\n12\tlanguage: en\n13\taudiences:\n14\t  - contributors\n15\tintent: Read a manni meta error, map it to the field and line, fix it, and confirm green locally.\n16\tlifecycle: published\n17\tapplies-to:\n18\t  - domain:meta\n19\trelated-pages:\n20\t  - meta-reference\n21\t  - meta-schemas\n22\tconcepts:\n23\t  - validation\n24\t  - frontmatter\n25\t  - schema\n26\trisks:\n27\t  - destructive\n28\tsample-questions:\n29\t  - What does this manni meta error line mean?\n30\t  - How do I fix a missing required field?\n31\t  - Why does my check exit 2 instead of 1?\n32\tgraph:\n33\t  label: Fix a failing check\n34\t  type: troubleshooting\n35\tlast-updated: 2026-10-20\n36\ttags:\n37\t  - validation\n38\t  - error-messages\n39\t  - troubleshooting\n40\t  - frontmatter\n41\t  - ci\n42\taction: troubleshoot\n43\tprerequisites:\n44\t  - meta-reference\n45\t  - /manni/meta/get-started/\n46\tnext-steps:\n47\t  - meta-reference\n48\t  - meta-schemas\n49\tverified-by:\n50\t  - tool: doc-detective\n51\t    check: fix-a-failing-check\n52\t---\n53\t\n54\timport { Steps, Aside, LinkCard } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';\n55\t\n56\tYour PR's manni meta check is red and you'd like it green again. You're in the\n57\tright place. This page decodes the error, and points you at the exact field and\n58\tline to change. It also shows you how to confirm the fix locally before you\n59\tre-push. You don't need to know how manni meta was set up, only what its output is\n60\ttelling you.\n61\t\n62\t<Aside type=\"tip\" title=\"The fastest path\">\n63\t  Find your error message in the [common failures](#common-failures) below, apply\n64\t  the matching fix, then [run manni meta locally](#reproduce-and-confirm-locally) to\n65\t  confirm it's green. Done.\n66\t</Aside>\n67\t\n68\t## Decode the error line\n69\t\n70\t{/* cite pretty-is-the-default-format */}\n71\tA failing file in `pretty` output (the default) looks like this:\n72\t\n73\t```\n74\t✗ docs/guide.md\n75\t    (root)  must have required property 'type'  [google:okf:0.1]\n76\t      google:okf:0.1 type: A short string identifying the kind of concept.\n77\t      Guide: https://hawkeyexl.github.io/manni/meta/reference/schemas/google-okf/\n78\t```\n79\t\n80\tThe first line is the file that failed. Each indented line below it is one\n81\tproblem, in this shape:\n82\t\n83\t```\n84\t<field>  <severity> <message>  (line N)  [schema-id]\n85\t  <schema-id> <property>: <what the property is for>\n86\t  Guide: <url>\n87\t```\n88\t\n89\t| Part | What it tells you |\n90\t| --- | --- |\n91\t| `<field>` | Which field is wrong. It's a [JSON Pointer](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6901) such as `/timestamp`, or a bare key name. `(root)` means the document as a whole, most often a *required field is missing entirely*. |\n92\t| `<severity>` | `warning ` or `notice ` when the fi\n…"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"046852b5-0926-411b-99aa-6a37cf88b6b9","uuid":"1f4ce6d7-2051-4f76-9898-74a020e595d0","timestamp":"2026-10-23T14:48:53.716Z","tool_use_result":{"trimmed":true},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014JT5kCQjtWFasBXkwT2num","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
